  "findings": [
    "Bounded support: tentative iterator traversal reaches commands behind unknown prefixes; fresh repeated commands, nested supported styles, escaping, no-closing-angle controls, Unicode boundaries and style restoration pass. Fresh valid membership is 7/8 after versus 1/8 before, with no lost pass.",
    "Counterexample empty_bold_recognition: Java paints A<outer, then bold </b>>B, then bold C; Rust paints A<outer>B and C. Canvas widths are Java217, before243, after179. CommandCreoleStyle.matchingSize returns the captured body length; the closed <b></b> alternative has length0, so StripeSimple.searchCommand rejects that candidate. CommandCreoleBuilder orders legacy then EOL; the EOL alternative recognizes the nonempty remaining </b>>B<$seed>C body. Rust handle_tag recognizes b solely by tag name and walk_with consumes through </b> even when the body is empty. The iterator is tentative, but its recognition predicate is not Java-equivalent.",
    "This handler mismatch predates the correction; the corrected outer-prefix reachability exposes it. The fresh whole-output failure rejects acceptance without implying a new lost pass or authorizing production changes.",
    "malformed_dot is a Java NumberFormatException SVG with exit0 and no timeout. It is nonpositive, not a valid passing diagram. Rust must not be made to panic to imitate the exception. It is preserved and registered, with result fail for the evidence schema but excluded from the25-valid denominator.",
    "No fixture text, branch-count ladders, new geometry constants or coordinate surgery found in the three-file production diff. The unknown-candidate flush occurs before recognition, but same-style coalescing preserves ordinary runs in the tested controls; sprite barriers remain explicit."
  ],
